{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788032075803010001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"paternal-repayable-flamingo","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"4d2be4857ea98d020cedc3d380bdc416a8607e776d7fdeed0b1604fbd62a2ac2","event_uuid":"40032e8a-3c4c-44ad-98e1-36e26bcbb5f5","position":{"commit_sha":"f1eaed5b835062675563560f9588482b1cfa8e9d","position":"1788029375846565150-40032e8a-3c4c-44ad-98e1-36e26bcbb5f5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"7d7d76105ff2a295da78a9d9b5125edcd593f9c7bd58a361bf2dad79f6167b4f","event_uuid":"38ddfd64-892d-4915-97a4-b1ec0b63500e","position":{"commit_sha":"72ef3878d1b5ce7f945b27fcd51317d450a1c972","position":"1788029390062310426-38ddfd64-892d-4915-97a4-b1ec0b63500e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0ff221b00118ae0b1cfd6c90a46e0624b65a7c92b9609981b0a4862080fe4901","event_uuid":"46de33a6-0ff3-43b4-bc41-7fc48eb65db0","position":{"commit_sha":"0d204bb93047f714b94d9cbfa2ae70e211fe57b2","position":"1788029402033528151-46de33a6-0ff3-43b4-bc41-7fc48eb65db0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"579f9a25c12e2c5d2f58f35c1d1bf33e4cb9260991b5deccd23e762366c85e9e","event_uuid":"d2047d93-3836-4c6b-a50c-23375e1e0999","position":{"commit_sha":"6fa253581afa368c0504d3adadf411d8d180215b","position":"1788029619110037273-d2047d93-3836-4c6b-a50c-23375e1e0999"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788029375846565150,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"38ddfd64-892d-4915-97a4-b1ec0b63500e","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877"},{"link_uuid":"46de33a6-0ff3-43b4-bc41-7fc48eb65db0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"efd4-847d-f7ad-47bc"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDaily plan-review cache reads in `.rebar/usage.jsonl` went from ~80% of input tokens (2026-08-06..11) to 0 from 2026-08-12 onward, and the median full plan review went from about $2.18 to about $4.82 (Aug 6–29 logged spend is roughly $3,000, of which finders alone are ~358M uncached Opus input tokens). The change coincides with commit `6d4f394195b2` (2026-08-10) adding the Anthropic-direct fallback to the frontier/standard classes in `rebar.toml` `[llm.model_classes]`. `_intersect_capabilities` in `src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py` intersects capabilities across the whole chain and collapses differing `prompt_cache_style` values to `\"none\"` — exactly the hazard the comment in `rebar.toml` around the caching keys warns about. So every call on a mixed chain runs uncached even though the primary Bedrock target supports caching.\n\n## Approach\n\nInvestigate before fixing (`/rebar-debug`): confirm with a unit reproduction that a chain `[bedrock:…opus, anthropic:…opus]` yields `prompt_cache_style=none` while the single-provider chain yields the Bedrock style; confirm from usage rows that the fallback almost never actually fires. Then pick one: (a) intersect capabilities only over providers that can actually serve the current call (primary first; fallback capabilities apply only after a fallback), or (b) make the chains homogeneous in `rebar.toml`. Default to (a) unless it destabilises the provider seam.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py`\n- `rebar.toml` (only if option b)\n- `tests/unit/test_runner_support.py`\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: mixed chain keeps the primary provider's cache style until a fallback actually occurs. Live check: one `review-plan` after the fix shows `cache_read_tokens > 0` on second and later finder calls.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A regression test proves a mixed chain no longer collapses `prompt_cache_style` to none for the primary target; checked in `make test`.\n- [ ] After the fix, a production plan review logs non-zero `cache_read_tokens`; checked in `.rebar/usage.jsonl`.\n- [ ] The root cause and the chosen option are recorded on this ticket.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py","reason":"capability intersection across the fallback chain"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_runner_support.py","reason":"regression test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","efd4-847d-f7ad-47bc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["llm","cost","bedrock","prompt-caching"],"ticket_id":"96f3-af59-ba26-4159","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Prompt caching silently disabled since 2026-08-12: mixed Bedrock+Anthropic class fallback collapses prompt_cache_style to none (~2x review cost)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["40032e8a-3c4c-44ad-98e1-36e26bcbb5f5","38ddfd64-892d-4915-97a4-b1ec0b63500e","46de33a6-0ff3-43b4-bc41-7fc48eb65db0","d2047d93-3836-4c6b-a50c-23375e1e0999"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788032075803010001,"uuid":"05b4fb90-1e4b-4ab8-a8d5-f6d7fe10ce64"}